[size=5]Description[/size]
Combat Text adds health bars, floating damage numbers, and status icons to zombies. The bars show how much health they have left, and the numbers show how much health each attack takes away.

Armored zombies also have blue segments below their health bar, one for each armor plate. These appear once the zombie takes health or armor damage. Each segment shrinks as the plate takes damage and empties when it breaks. Hits that cause no health loss do not produce a damage number.

[size=5]Main features[/size]
[list]
[*]A health bar above each damaged zombie, hidden while it is at full health and gone when it dies.
[*]Floating numbers show health lost to attacks and fire damage.
[*]Blue segments show how much armor remains on each plate.
[*]A broken-shield icon flashes above the health bar when the last armor plate breaks.
[*]Fire, bleed, and stun icons appear beside the health bar and turn gray as the effects wear off.
[*]Repeated damage of the same type to the same zombie adds up in one number when it occurs close together.
[*]Settings to toggle bars and numbers, adjust bar, number, and icon sizes, and choose how long numbers stay visible.
[/list]

[size=5]Requirements[/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thelaststandaftermath/mods/1]BepInEx for The Last Stand: Aftermath[/url]. Install it first.
[/list]

[size=5]Installation[/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thelaststandaftermath/mods/1]BepInEx[/url] [i](if no other mods were installed before, start the game once so BepInEx finishes setup, then quit)[/i].
[*]Extract this mod's zip into the game folder (the folder with the game .exe). The DLL lands in BepInEx\plugins. Full path examples:
[list]
[*]Steam: [code]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\The Last Stand Aftermath\BepInEx\plugins\CombatText.dll[/code]
[*]Epic: [code]C:\Program Files\Epic Games\The Last Stand Aftermath\BepInEx\plugins\CombatText.dll[/code]
[/list]
[/list]

[size=5]Uninstall[/size]
Delete CombatText.dll from the BepInEx\plugins folder.

[size=5]Configuration[/size]
To change mod settings, edit [font=Courier New]BepInEx\config\com.ivmakk.tlsa.combattext.cfg[/font] (see [url=https://github.com/ivmakk-tlsa/tlsa-combat-text/blob/main/CONFIG.md]CONFIG.md[/url] for every setting).

